    "narrative": "For Ghost Ride the WHIP\u2019s June 30th slate, **Mickey Moniak** (75.74) and **Seiya Suzuki** (72.64) anchor our attack, representing our strongest starts. **Mickey Moniak** benefits from a massive 14% boost via platoon splits and an additional 5% bump from favorable wind conditions, making him an elite play against the vulnerable Eury P\u00e9rez. Meanwhile, **Seiya Suzuki** is maximized by a soft matchup against the 4.56 xERA of Sears and the same beneficial wind profile. **Brice Turang** also earns a high-tier nod (71.09) due to his premier position in the order and a favorable 19% SP skill adjustment against Lowder, providing necessary stability for our Roto floor.\n\nStolen base upside remains our primary driver, and while **Corbin Carroll** (70.86) faces the slightly tougher Roupp, his sprint speed and order placement are non-negotiable. **James Wood** (58.14) and **Henry Bolte** (61.60) both draw favorable park factors and the \"Slow SP Delivery\" bonus, which increases their SB probability significantly against their respective opponents. The most difficult bench decision involved **Isaac Paredes** (48.59). He was the closest to cracking the starting nine, but his negative SP skill adjustment against Ryan and a lower efficiency rating compared to the heavy platoon-advantage starts for **Max Muncy** and **Austin Riley** relegated him to the bench for today's rotation.\n\nManagers should monitor the lineup for **Dalton Rushing**, whose score (47.71) is hampered by an unfavorable platoon matchup against the lefty Springs. While he remains above our 40-point \"Below Floor\" threshold, he is the most volatile asset in today's lineup. We are also wary of **Gabriel Moreno** facing Roupp; while his score (57.41) is solid, he sits right on the edge of marginal utility. Outside of the active lineup, **Travis Bazzana** (40.14) barely escaped the \"Below Floor\" designation, but his matchup against deGrom makes him a high-risk hold that the optimizer correctly opted to avoid in favor of more consistent daily efficiency.",
